msgid "Process a raw Apple iCloud Photos export before importing it into another photo service."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process a raw Apple iCloud Photos export before importing it into another photo service. This feature reads Photo Details.csv metadata, restores dates into photos and videos, rebuilds Albums from Apple CSV collections, and writes a portable output library with ALL_PHOTOS and Albums. When enabled, Memories CSV collections are also reconstructed as album-like folders. IMPORTANT: This module is a local preprocessing pipeline. It does not push anything to a cloud target by itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process a raw Google Photos Takeout export before importing it into another photo service."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process a raw Google Photos Takeout export before importing it into another photo service. This feature repairs dates and metadata, rebuilds album membership from sidecar JSON files, organizes the output into ALL_PHOTOS and Albums, and can optionally create symbolic album entries instead of duplicating files. When the input is an album-only Takeout with no year folders, PhotoMigrator detects it automatically and switches GPTH to the appropriate recovery flow. IMPORTANT: This module is a local preprocessing pipeline. It does not push anything to a cloud target by itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process a revised duplicates CSV and execute actions from the 'Action' column."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process a revised duplicates CSV and execute actions from the 'Action' column. Use this after '--find-duplicates' to apply manual decisions in your reviewed CSV. Valid actions: restore_duplicate / remove_duplicate / replace_duplicate. IMPORTANT: remove_duplicate and replace_duplicate are irreversible operations. Example: --process-duplicates ./Duplicates/Duplicates_revised.csv"
msgstr ""

msgid "Process an Apple iCloud Photos export folder <ICLOUD_EXPORT_FOLDER> to recover dates from 'Photo Details.csv' files, assign those dates to the media files, and organize assets."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process an Apple iCloud Photos export folder <ICLOUD_EXPORT_FOLDER> to recover dates from 'Photo Details.csv' files, assign those dates to the media files, and organize assets. If any ZIP file is found inside it, the ZIPs will be extracted first into '<ICLOUD_EXPORT_FOLDER>_unzipped_<TIMESTAMP>', and that folder will be used as input. The processed export will be saved into the folder '<ICLOUD_EXPORT_FOLDER>_processed_<TIMESTAMP>'."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process it and let me download the result."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process the Takeout folder <TAKEOUT_FOLDER> to fix all metadata and organize assets inside it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Process the Takeout folder <TAKEOUT_FOLDER> to fix all metadata and organize assets inside it. If any Zip file is found inside it, the Zip will be extracted to the folder '<TAKEOUT_FOLDER>_unzipped_<TIMESTAMP>', and that folder will be used as input. The processed Takeout will be saved into the folder '<TAKEOUT_FOLDER>_processed_<TIMESTAMP>'. This argument is mandatory to run the Google Takeout Processor feature."
msgstr ""

